# ⚠ The comment above stated the intent from the start, but the patterns only
#    ever covered PRODUCT/DESIGN — the skill's OWN output directory was never
#    listed. Result: on 2026-08-19 `.impeccable/critique/*.md` was committed and
#    served publicly (HTTP 200, text/markdown) on the indexed surface. Fixed.
.impeccable/

# ── NON-FUNCTIONAL TO THE SERVED SITE — untracked 2026-08-19 (Marco).
#    The rule this whole file exists for: every tracked file is served as public
#    plain text. So the test for tracking is not "is it useful?" but "does the
#    browser need it to render a page?" Nothing below is referenced by any
#    href/src/url in any shipped HTML/CSS/JS — verified before removal.
#    All of it stays on disk; only git stops carrying it.
scripts/          # .docx generators + image optimiser. Authoring tooling, and
                  # they embed internal deliverable names and page context.
design/           # internal design working docs (brandguide token extraction,
                  # per-vertical accent proposal, type-scale notes, references).
README.md         # stale: describes the Automotive vertical, names internal
                  # skill paths, and documents a known production bug publicly.
webflow.config.json  # Webflow CLI deploy config; exposes the Webflow siteId.
                     # The four verticals are closed and client-owned, so this
                     # is historical tooling, not part of any live build.
